== labels_of_a_frame
error[Z0401]: `labels` cannot be called on a Frame
 --> scripts/main.zeff:3:1
  |
3 | d.labels(title: "A frame")
  | ^ this is a Frame
  |
  = help: `labels` takes a Plot first; `x.labels(...)` is `labels(x, ...)`

== a_title_that_leaves_no_room
error[Z0401]: a page of 89 by 66 mm is too small for this plot: its labels, never set below 8 points, leave 65 by 6.2 mm for the panel
 --> scripts/main.zeff:3:1
  |
3 | export(p.labels(title: "A title of many words that runs on and on well past the right edge of a figure one column wide and then some more and more and more until the lines it takes fill the page from its top to its foot and leave nothing at all for the panel which is after all the point of a figure and should be given the room that these words take from it line after line after line after line after line after line after line after line after line after line after line after line after line after line after line"), "long.svg")
  | ^^^^^^ too small a page
  |
  = help: a panel needs 12.7 mm each way; give a larger `size:`, as `one_column` (89 by 66 mm) or `two_column` (183 by 110 mm), or shorten the labels
